{
  "title": "45: al-Jaaseyah الجاثية",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nحٰمٓ‌‌ ۚ‏(1)\nHAA-MEEM.\nHa. Mim. (H. M.)\nتَنْزِيْلُ الْكِتٰبِ مِنَ اللّٰهِ الْعَزِيْزِ الْحَكِيْمِ‏(2)\nTANZEELU KETAABE MENAL LAAHE A’ZEEZIL HAKEEM.\nThe descent (or revealed) of the Book (Qur’an) from God, the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.\nاِنَّ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَؕ‏(3)\nINNAL FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE LA-AAYAATIL LLELMUMENEENA.\nVerily in the heavens and the earth are signs for the believers.\nوَفِىْ خَلْقِكُمْ وَمَا يَبُثُّ مِنْ دَآبَّةٍ اٰيٰتٌ لِّقَوْمٍ يُّوْقِنُوْنَۙ‏(4)\nWA FEE KHALQEKUM WA MAA YABUSSU MIN DAAAB-BATIL AAYAATUM LEQAWMINY YOOQENOON.\nAnd in your (own) creation, and what He scattereth in the earth, of the animals, are signs for a people sure in faith,\nوَاخْتِلَافِ الَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ وَمَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مِنْ رِّزْقٍ فَاَحْيَا بِهِ الْاَرْضَ بَعْدَ مَوْتِهَا وَ تَصْرِيْفِ الرِّيٰحِ اٰيٰتٌ لِّقَوْمٍ يَّعْقِلُوْنَ‏(5)\nWAKHTELAAFIL LAYLE WAN NAHAARE WA MAA ANZALAL LAAHO MENAL SAMAAA-E MIN RREZQIN FA-AHYAA BEHIL ARZA BA’DA MAWTEHAA WA TASREEFE REYAAHE AAYAATUM LEQAWMINY YA’QELOON.\nAnd in the alternation of the night and the day, and what God sendeth down from heaven, of the sustenance, and (in His) giving life thereby to the earth after its death, and (in) the changing of the winds, are signs for a people who understand.\nتِلْكَ اٰيٰتُ اللّٰهِ نَتْلُوْهَا عَلَيْكَ بِالْحَقِّ‌ ‌ۚ فَبِاَىِّ حَدِيْثٍۢ بَعْدَ اللّٰهِ وَاٰيٰتِهٖ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(6)\nTILKA AAYAATUL LAAHE NATLOOHAA A’LAYKA BIL-HAQQE FABE-AYYE HADEESIN BA’DA LAAHE WA AAYAATEHI YOAMENOONA.\nThese are the signs of God recite We unto thee with truth; then in what (other) argument after (rejecting) God and His signs, would they believe?\nوَيْلٌ لِّكُلِّ اَفَّاكٍ اَثِيْمٍۙ‏(7)\nWAYLUL LEKULLE AAFFAAKIN ASEEM.\nWoe unto every liar, (and every) sinner,\nيَّسْمَعُ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِ ثُمَّ يُصِرُّ مُسْتَكْبِرًا كَاَنْ لَّمْ يَسْمَعْهَا‌ ۚ فَبَشِّرْهُ بِعَذَابٍ اَ لِيْمٍ‏(8)\nYYASMAU’U AAYAATIL LAAHE TUTLAA A’LAYHE SUMMA YUSERRU MUSTAKBERAN KA-AN LAM YASMAA’HAA BE BE-A’ZAABIN A’ZAABAN LEEMIN.\nHe heareth the signs of God recited unto him, yet persisteth he arrogantly, as if he hath heard them not; so announce thou unto them a painful chastisement.\nوَاِذَا عَلِمَ مِنْ اٰيٰتِنَا شَيْئًا اۨتَّخَذَهَا هُزُوًا‌ ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ مُّهِيْنٌ ؕ‏(9)\nWA EZAA A’LEMA MIN AAYAATENAA SHAY-ANW ATTAKHAZAHAA HOZOWANW OOLAAA-EKA LAHUM A’ZAABUN MOHEEN.\nAnd when he cometh to know any of Our signs he taketh it in jest; These shall have a disgracing chastisement.\nمِنْ وَّرَآئِهِمْ جَهَنَّمُۚ وَلَا يُغْنِىْ عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَسَبُوْا شَيْئًا وَّلَا مَا اتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اَوْلِيَآءَ‌ ۚ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ عَظِيْمٌؕ‏(10)\nMIN WA-RAAA-EHIM JAHANNAMUL WA LAA YUGHNEE A’NHUM MAA KASABOO SHAY-ANW WA LAA MAA ATTAKHAZOOA MIN DOONIL LAAHE AAWLEEAAAA WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN A’AZEEMUN.\nBehind them is hell, and shall avail them not aught of what they did earn, nor those whom they took as guardians besides God, and for them shall be a grievous chastisement.\nهٰذَا هُدًى‌ ‌ۚ وَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ مِّنْ رِّجْزٍ اَلِيْمٌ‏(11)\nHAAZAA HODAM WAL LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-AAYAATIL RABBEHIM LAHUM A’ZAABUN MIN RREJZIN ALEEM.\nThis (Qur’an) is guidance, and those who disbelieve in the signs of their Lord, for them shall be the most painful chastisement.\nاَللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ سَخَّرَ لَكُمُ الْبَحْرَ لِتَجْرِىَ الْفُلْكُ فِيْهِ بِاَمْرِهٖ وَلِتَبْتَغُوْا مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ وَلَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(12)\nALLAAHO LAZEE SAKKHARA LAKOMUL BAHRA LETAJREAAA FULKO FEEHE LAAHO WA LETABTAGHOO MIN FAZLEHI WA LA-A’LLAKUM TASHKOROON.\nGod is He Who made subservient unto you the sea that may traverse the ships therein by His command, and that ye may seek of His grace and that ye may be thankful.\nوَسَخَّرَ لَكُمْ مَّا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ جَمِيْعًا مِّنْهُ‌ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يَّتَفَكَّرُوْنَ‏(13)\nSAKHKHARASH LAKUM MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE JAMEE-A’A MINHO INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMINY YATAFAKKAROON.\nAnd made subservient unto you whatsoever is in the heavens and whatsoever is in the earth, all, on His behalf: Verily in this are signs for people who reflect.\nقُلْ لِّلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا يَغْفِرُوْا لِلَّذِيْنَ لَا يَرْجُوْنَ اَيَّامَ اللّٰهِ لِيَجْزِىَ قَوْمًۢا بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(14)\nQUL LIL-LAZEENA AAMANOO YAGHFEROOA LILLAZEENA LAA YARJOON AAYAMA LAAHE LE-YAJZEYAL QAWMAN BEMAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) unto those (that) they may forgive those who hope not the days of God, that He may recompense the people for what they earn\nمَنْ عَمِلَ صَالِحًا فَلِنَفْسِهٖ‌ۚ وَمَنْ اَسَآءَ فَعَلَيْهَا ثُمَّ اِلٰى رَبِّكُمْ تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(15)\nMAN A’MELA SAALEHAN FALENAFSEH WA MAN ASAAA-A FA A’LAYHAA SUMMA ELAA RABBEKUM TURJA-O’ON.\nWhoever doeth good, it is for his own self, and whoever doeth evil, it is against his own self; then unto your Lord ye shall be returned.\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ الْكِتٰبَ وَالْحُكْمَ وَالنُّبُوَّةَ وَرَزَقْنٰهُمْ مِّنَ الطَّيِّبٰتِ وَفَضَّلْنٰهُمْ عَلَى الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(16)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ KETAABA WAL HUKMA WA NOBUWWATA WA RAZAQNAAHUM MENAL AT-TAYBAATE WAFAZZALNAAHUM A’LAL A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd indeed, gave We the children of Israel, the Book, and Wisdom and the Prophethood, and provided them with sustenance from the goodly things, and We favoured them above all peoples.\nوَاٰتَيْنٰهُمْ بَيِّنٰتٍ مِّنَ الْاَمْرِ‌ ۚ فَمَا اخْتَلَفُوْۤا اِلَّا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا جَآءَهُمُ الْعِلْمُ ۙ بَغْيًاۢ بَيْنَهُمْ‌ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ يَقْضِىْ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ فِيْمَا كَانُوْا فِيْهِ يَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(17)\nWA AATAYNAAHUM BAYYENAAT MENAL AL-AAMRE FAMAA TALAFOO ILLAA MIN BA’DE MAA JAAA-AHOMUL I’LMO BAGHYAN BAYNAHUM INNAL RABBAKA YAQZEE BAYNAHUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE FEEMAA KAANOO FEEHE YAKHTALEFOON.\nAnd We gave them clear arguments of the affair but they differed not until knowledge hath come unto them, through rivalry among themselves; Verily thy Lord will judge between them on the Day of Reckoning, about that wherein they differ.\nثُمَّ جَعَلْنٰكَ عَلٰى شَرِيْعَةٍ مِّنَ الْاَمْرِ فَاتَّبِعْهَا وَلَا تَتَّبِعْ اَهْوَآءَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(18)\nSUMMA JAA’ALNAAKA A’LAA SHAREEA’ATIN MENAL AL-AAMRE FAATTABEA’HAA WA LAA TATTABEA’ AAHWAAA LAZEENA LAA YA’LAMOON.\nThen have We set thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) on a (definite) course of Law, so follow it, and follow not the vain desires of those who know not.\nاِنَّهُمْ لَنْ يُّغْنُوْا عَنْكَ مِنَ اللّٰهِ شَيْئًا‌ ؕ وَ اِنَّ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ بَعْضُهُمْ اَوْلِيَآءُ بَعْضٍ‌ ۚ وَاللّٰهُ وَلِىُّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(19)\nINNAHUM LAN YYUGHNOOA A’NKAL MENAL LAAHE SHAY-ANW WA INNAL ZAALEMEEN KHALAA ANNAKUM AWLEYAAA-O ELAA WAL LAAHO WALIYYUL MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nVerily, they shall avail not thee aught against God; And verily, the unjust are the friends of one another; and God is the guardian of the pious ones.\nهٰذَا بَصَائِرُ لِلنَّاسِ وَهُدًى وَّرَحْمَةٌ لِّقَوْمٍ يُّوْقِنُوْنَ‏(20)\nHAAZAA BASAAERU LIN-NAASE WA HODANW WA RAHMATUL LEQAWMINY YOOQENOON.\nThese are proofs for the people and a guidance and a mercy unto a people who are sure in faith.\nاَمْ حَسِبَ الَّذِيْنَ اجْتَرَحُوا السَّيِّاٰتِ اَنْ نَّجْعَلَهُمْ كَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ ۙ سَوَآءً مَّحْيَاهُمْ وَمَمَاتُهُمْ‌ ؕ سَآءَ مَا يَحْكُمُوْنَ‏(21)\nAM HASEBA LAZEENA AJTARAHOOA SAYYE-AATE AN NNAJA’ALAHUM TAKOONOO AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE SAWAAAN MMAHYAAHUM WAMAMAATUHUM SAAA-A MAA YAHKUMOONA.\nWhat! deem those who have wrought evils that We will make them like unto those who believe and do good, that equal shall be their life and their death? (Nay!) ill it is what they judge.\nوَ خَلَقَ اللّٰهُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ بِالْحَقِّ وَلِتُجْزٰى كُلُّ نَفْسٍۢ بِمَا كَسَبَتْ وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(22)\nWA KHALAQAL LAAHO SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA BIL-HAQQE WALETUJZAA KULLO NAFSIM BEMAA KASABAT WA HUM LAA LAA YUZLAMOON.\nAnd created God, the heavens and the earth with the truth, and that be recompensed every soul for what it hath earned, and they shall not be done (the least) injustice.\nاَفَرَءَيْتَ مَنِ اتَّخَذَ اِلٰهَهٗ هَوٰٮهُ وَاَضَلَّهُ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى عِلْمٍ وَّخَتَمَ عَلٰى سَمْعِهٖ وَقَلْبِهٖ وَجَعَلَ عَلٰى بَصَرِهٖ غِشٰوَةً  ؕ فَمَنْ يَّهْدِيْهِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ اللّٰهِ‌ ؕ اَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(23)\nAAFARAAYTA MANIS TAKHAZA AELAAHAH HAWHU WAAZALLAHU LAAHO A’LAA I’LMIN WWAKHATAMA A’LAA SAME’EH WA QALBEHI WA A’LAA BASAREH GHESHAAWATAN FAMAN YYAHDEEHE MIN BA’DE LAAHE AFALAA TAZAKKAROON.\nHast thou then seen him who taketh as his god his vain desires, and God hath allowed him to be astray (with his), knowing (it), and set a seal upon his ear and his heart and caused upon his eyes a veil; who can guide him after (his being allowed to stray by) God? What! Will ye not then reflect?\nوَقَالُوْا مَا هِىَ اِلَّا حَيَاتُنَا الدُّنْيَا نَمُوْتُ وَنَحْيَا وَمَا يُهْلِكُنَاۤ اِلَّا الدَّهْرُ‌ؕ وَمَا لَهُمْ بِذٰلِكَ مِنْ عِلْمٍ‌ ۚ اِنْ هُمْ اِلَّا يَظُنُّوْنَ‏(24)\nWA QAALOO MAA HEYA ILLAA HAYAATUNAA DUNYAA NAMOOTU WANAHYAA WA MAA YUHLEKUNAA ILLAA AD-DAHRU WA MAA LAHUM BE-ZAALEKA MIN I’LMIN IN HUM ILLAA YAZUNNOONA.\nAnd say they: “Naught it is save our life in this world; we die and live and destroyeth us not but time.” For them there is no knowledge of that; they do but (merely) guess.\nوَاِذَا تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتُنَا بَيِّنٰتٍ مَّا كَانَ حُجَّتَهُمْ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ قَالُوا ائْتُوْا بِاٰبَآئِنَاۤ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(25)\nWA EZAA TUTLAA A’LAYHIM AAYAATONAA BAYYENAAT MAA KAANA HUJJATAHUM ILLAA AN QAALUD ATOOA BE-AABAAA-ENAA IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nAnd when are recited unto them Our clear signs, nothing is their argument but they only say: “Bring ye our fathers (back) if ye be truthful.\nقُلِ اللّٰهُ يُحْيِيْكُمْ ثُمَّ يُمِيْتُكُمْ ثُمَّ يَجْمَعُكُمْ اِلٰى يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ لَا رَيْبَ فِيْهِ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(26)\nQOLIL LAAHO YOHYEEKUM SUMMA YOMEETOKUM SUMMA YAJMAU’UKUM ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE LAA RAYBA FEEHE LAAKINNAL AKSARAN NAASE LAA YA’LAMOON.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “God giveth you life then he causeth you to die, then will He gather you unto the Day of Reckoning, about which there is no doubt, but most people know not.\nوَلِلّٰهِ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ؕ وَيَوْمَ تَقُوْمُ السَّاعَةُ يَوْمَئِذٍ يَّخْسَرُ الْمُبْطِلُوْنَ‏(27)\nLILLAAHE MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ WA YAWMA YAQOOMUS SAA-A’TO YAWMA-EZIN YYAKHSARU MUBTELOON.\nAnd God’s is the kingdom of the heavens and the earth; and on the day when the Hour (of Reckoning) shall be established, on that Day shall lose the believers in the falsehood.\nوَتَرٰى كُلَّ اُمَّةٍ جَاثِيَةً‌ كُلُّ اُمَّةٍ تُدْعٰۤى اِلٰى كِتٰبِهَا ؕ اَلْيَوْمَ تُجْزَوْنَ مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(28)\nWATARAA KULLA UMMATIN JAASEETAN KULLO UMMATIN TUDA’AA ELAA KETAABEHAA AL-YAWMA TUJZAWNA MAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nAnd thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) shalt see every people kneeling down; every people shall be called unto its Book; Today ye shall be recompensed for what all ye used to do.\nهٰذَا كِتٰبُنَا يَنْطِقُ عَلَيْكُمْ بِالْحَقِّ‌ؕ اِنَّا كُنَّا نَسْتَنْسِخُ مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(29)\nHAAZAA KETAABUNAA YANTEQU A’LAYKUM BIL-HAQ INNAA KUNNAA NASTANSEKHU MAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nThis is Our Book that speaketh against you with justice; verily, We used to record whatever ye used to do.\nفَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ فَيُدْخِلُهُمْ رَبُّهُمْ فِىْ رَحْمَتِهٖ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ هُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(30)\nFA-AMMAA LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE FAYUDKHELUHUM RABBOHUM FEE FEE ZAA LEKA HOWA FAWZUL MOBEEN.\nAnd those who believed and did good deeds, so will admit them their Lord into His mercy, that is the manifest achievement.\nوَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اَفَلَمْ تَكُنْ اٰيٰتِىْ تُتْلٰى عَلَيْكُمْ فَاسْتَكْبَرْتُمْ وَكُنْتُمْ قَوْمًا مُّجْرِمِيْنَ‏(31)\nWA AMMAA LAZEENA KAFAROO A-FALAM TAKUN AAAYAATEAA TUTLAA A’LAYKUM FA TAKBARTUM WA KUNTUM QAWMAN MMUJREMEENA.\nAnd those who disbelieved: (unto them will be said): “What! were not My signs recited unto you? But ye acted arrogantly and ye were a guilty people.\nوَاِذَا قِيْلَ اِنَّ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقٌّ وَّالسَّاعَةُ لَا رَيْبَ فِيْهَا قُلْتُمْ مَّا نَدْرِىْ مَا السَّاعَةُ ۙ اِنْ نَّظُنُّ اِلَّا ظَنًّا وَّمَا نَحْنُ بِمُسْتَيْقِنِيْنَ‏(32)\nWA EZAA QEELA INNAL WA’DAL LAAHE HAQQUWN WWAALSSAAA’ATU LAA RAYBA FEEHAA IZ QULTUM MAA NADREAA MAA SAA-A’TO IN NNAZUNNU ILLAA ZANNAN WA MAA NAHNO BEMUSTAYQENEENA.\nAnd it was said (unto them): “Verily, the promise of God is true and the Hour (of Reckoning), no doubt is there about it, ye said ‘We know not what the Hour is,’ we deem it naught but a mere guess, and we are not sure.\nوَبَدَا لَهُمْ سَيِّاٰتُ مَا عَمِلُوْا وَحَاقَ بِهِمْ مَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(33)\nWABADAA LAHUM SAYAAATU MAA A’MELOO WAHAAQA BEHIM MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZEOON.\nAnd shall manifest unto them the evils of what they wrought, and shall surround them that which they used to mock at.\nوَقِيْلَ الْيَوْمَ نَنْسٰٮكُمْ كَمَا نَسِيْتُمْ لِقَآءَ يَوْمِكُمْ هٰذَا وَمَاْوٰٮكُمُ النَّارُ وَمَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ نّٰصِرِيْنَ‏(34)\nWA QEELAD YAWMA NANSAAKUM KAMAA NASEETUM LE-QAAA-AL YAWMEKUM HAAZAA WAMAAWAAKUMU TAMASSANAN WA MAA LAKUM MIN NAASEREEN.\nAnd it shall be said (unto them): “Today We neglect you even as ye neglected the meeting of this day of yours and your abode shall be the fire, and for you shall not be any of the helpers\nذٰلِكُمْ بِاَنَّكُمُ اتَّخَذْتُمْ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ هُزُوًا وَّغَرَّتْكُمُ الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَا‌ ۚ فَالْيَوْمَ لَا يُخْرَجُوْنَ مِنْهَا وَلَا هُمْ يُسْتَعْتَبُوْنَ‏(35)\nZAALEKUM BEAANNAKUMU TAKHAZTUM AAYAATIL LAAHE HOZOWANW WWAGHARRATKUMU HAYAATUD DUNYAA FALYAWMA LAA YUKHRAJOONA MINHAA WA LAA HUM HUM YUSTA’TABOON.\nThat is for ye took the signs of God for a jest and deceived you, the life of this world “so on that day they shall not be taken out thence, nor shall they be granted any grace.\nفَلِلّٰهِ الْحَمْدُ رَبِّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَرَبِّ الْاَرْضِ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(36)\nFALILLAAHE HAMDO RABBE SAMAAWAATE WA RABBE ARZE RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nTherefore, God’s (alone) is the praise, the Lord of the heavens and the Lord of the earth, the Lord of the worlds.\nوَلَهُ الْكِبْرِيَآءُ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ وَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(37)\nLAHUL AL-KEBREEAAAU FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA HOWA A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nAnd His (only) is greatness in the heavens and the earth; and He is the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Jaaseyah (The Kneeling)\nThere are 37 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. This Surah is also called Surah al-Shari’ah. It is narrated that whoever recites this Surah will not be frightened on the Day of Judgement and his private parts will remain covered (whereas all people will be raised naked on this day).\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that whoever recites this Surah will not see Jahannam and neither will he hear the voice of its flames. Keeping this Surah in one’s possession makes him a beloved of the people and protects him from tyrant rulers. It also keeps one safe from those who love to slander and backbite. If it is placed on the neck of a newborn child, it ensures safety and protection from all calamities."
